course: dictionary
lesson: 12470
title: Deforestation
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Deforestation is a long word, but it has clues inside it. «Forest» is the main part, and «de-» often means taking something away. So deforestation is about taking forests away.
explain: Deforestation means cutting down or burning large areas of forest, so the trees are gone and the land is used for something else. «Every year, more of the rainforest is lost to deforestation.» The word «lost» tells you the forest is disappearing.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: «Every year, more of the rainforest is lost to cutting down and burning.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: Deforestation is an uncountable noun, so we say «deforestation», not «a deforestation».
fact: Forests are cleared for farms, cattle, palm oil, mining and wood.
fact: Deforestation destroys habitats, so animals lose their homes.
fact: When trees are gone, soil can wash away (erosion), and floods become more likely.
fact: Clearing forests adds carbon dioxide to the air, which makes climate change worse. Replanting trees (reforestation), protecting forests and buying sustainable wood all help.
exercise: «The company cut down the whole forest to make room for a palm oil farm.» What is this an example of? | *Deforestation | Erosion | Reforestation | Recycling
exercise: Which word means replanting trees so that a forest grows again? | Deforestation | Flood | *Reforestation | Desert
exercise: Which of these is a result of deforestation? | Soil is held more tightly by roots | *Animals lose their homes | Trees grow back faster | More rare birds nest in the cleared land
test: «Large areas of forest were burned so the land could be used for cattle.» Which word means the forest was cut down or burned? | Reforestation | Climate | *Deforestation | Habitat
test: Why does deforestation make climate change worse? | It stops the rain falling | It cools the air down | It makes more oxygen | *It adds carbon dioxide to the air
exam: Which of these is a sustainable solution to deforestation? | Burning more forest for land | Clearing more forest for farms | *Replanting trees (reforestation) | Using more palm oil in every product
